{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["And the reason of <b>For you are a holy people to YHWH your Elohim</b> is joined to <b>You shall not boil a kid in its mother's milk</b>, for it is not a detestable food, but He forbids it so that we may be holy in our foods, or that we may be holy so that we do not become a cruel people without mercy, who milk the mother and take from her the milk in which her young is cooked. And even though all meat in milk is included in this prohibition, for every nursing female is called 'mother' and every nursing young is called 'kid,' and this is the manner of cooking — and behold in all of them there is cruelty. And Rashi wrote (Rashi on Deuteronomy 14:21): 'You shall not boil a kid in its mother's milk' three times — to exclude the wild animal, the fowl, and the unclean beast. And they derived this midrash (Sifrei 103 and Hullin 113) from the word 'kid,' but the prohibition itself is one for the prohibition of eating, and one for the prohibition of deriving benefit, and one for the prohibition of cooking. And so the Rav wrote in the pericope 'And these are the judgments' (Exodus 23:19)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:49:54.916091847Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}